#Agent rules
1. The system is documented in the document folder under following documents. Please keep them up to date according to my input and feedback.
   1.1 description.md:
       - Provide concise description of the app or system idea
       - Document core use cases and features
   2.2 architecture.md:
       - Define full technical stack (frontend/backend frameworks, databases)
       - Testing frameworks and strategy
   3.3 datamodel.md:
       - Document all entities, attributes and relationships
   4.4 frontend.md:
       - List and describe all views/screens
       - Define UI/UX patterns and styling approach
   5.5 backend.md:
       - Document all API endpoints and authentication
       - Define service architecture and components
   6.6 todo.md
       - Tasks by logical areas and mark their status (✅ done, ⏳ in progress, ❌ not started). Next priority tasks in the end.
       - Prefer full stack tasks.
   6.7 ai_changelog.md
       - Changelog of changes done

2. When I say implement, please implement the code using following steps using chain of thoughts reasoning.
  2.1 REQUIRED: First read the needed documentation from the document folder
  2.2 Chain of thoughts must follow this format:
    1. "Reading required files..."
    2. "Analysis: what I found in the files..."
    3. "Plan: what needs to be done..."
    4. "Implementation: how I'll do it..."
  2.3 Scan the codebase for relevant files and methods first for getting context. Don't make assumptions.
  2.4 Place frontend code in the frontend directory and backend code in the backend directory
  2.5 Before proceeding with implementation:
    - Confirm all required files were read
    - List key findings from each file
    - Explain how these findings inform the implementation
3. When I say validate, please review and validate the code for correctness and execute the unit tests for it. If you don't have unit tests, please create them.
4. When I say record, write summary of what you did in the ai_changelog.md and update the todo list in the todo.md (do not remove any tasks, just update their status)
5. When I say invent, please implement a tool in the tools/ directory and write a tool description in .cursorrules file. Run it.
6. When I say design, please plan for the app or change and update all needed documentation
7. All frontend code goes user frontend folder and backend in backend folder. No not create anything but documentation under main folder


#Web Tools
The following command-line tools are available in the tools/ directory:

1. Web Search Tool (web_search.py):
   - Purpose: Search the web using DuckDuckGo API
   - Usage: ./web_search.py "your search query" [--max-results N] [--json]
   - Options:
     * --max-results: Maximum number of results to return (default: 5)
     * --json: Output results in JSON format

2. Web Reader Tool (web_reader.py):
   - Purpose: Read and parse webpage content
   - Usage: ./web_reader.py "https://example.com" [--json] [--content-only]
   - Options:
     * --json: Output results in JSON format
     * --content-only: Output only the main content

3. Image Optimizer Tool (image_optimizer.py):
   - Purpose: Optimize and scale images for responsive web use
   - Usage: ./image_optimizer.py input_image.jpg [--output-dir DIR] [--breakpoints W W W] [--quality Q]
   - Options:
     * --output-dir, -o: Output directory for processed images (default: optimized)
     * --breakpoints, -b: Custom width breakpoints in pixels (default: 640 1024 1920)
     * --quality, -q: Output image quality 0-100 (default: 85)
   - Features:
     * Generates WebP format with fallback images
     * Maintains aspect ratio during resizing
     * Optimizes file size and quality
     * Creates responsive image sets for mobile, tablet, and desktop

4. Image Describer Tool (image_describer.py):
   - Purpose: Analyze images using OpenAI's Vision API and generate descriptive filenames
   - Usage: ./image_describer.py image.jpg [--rename] [--json]
   - Options:
     * --rename: Automatically rename the file based on the AI description
     * --json: Output results in JSON format
   - Features:
     * Uses OpenAI's GPT-4 Vision API for detailed image analysis
     * Generates human-readable descriptions
     * Suggests descriptive filenames
     * Can automatically rename files based on content
   - Requirements:
     * Requires OpenAI API key in .env file
     * Supports common image formats (JPG, PNG, etc.)

